Subject: WTF/JSC: Phoenix machine context (SA_SIGINFO ucontext_t), concurrent GC on

Phoenix-RTOS delivers siginfo_t and a ucontext_t to SA_SIGINFO handlers on aarch64, with
Linux's uc_mcontext layout (fault_address, regs[31], sp, pc, pstate; <sys/ucontext.h>). So
HAVE(MACHINE_CONTEXT) on OS(PHOENIX) && CPU(ARM64), PlatformRegisters is the mcontext_t (the
Phoenix "no ucontext" case of 0002-wtf-threads-phoenix goes), and MachineContext.h reads it
through the Linux branches. Thread::suspend() now captures every general register of the
suspended thread, which is what a concurrent collector's conservative scan needs, so the
Phoenix override that kept useConcurrentGC false (0004-jsc-phoenix) goes too. FP/SIMD
registers are restored across a handler but not exposed in the mcontext_t (Linux's
__reserved area is not provided). With the DFG this also turns on SIGNAL_BASED_VM_TRAPS.

